                text: "**J Kumar** (Mumbai's elevated roads, metros and road tunnels), **Cemindia** (ports, metro tunnels, foundations and Adani group data centres), **Patel Engineering** (Himalayan dams and hydro tunnels) and **Afcons** (ports, bridges, tunnels and metros in India and ten other countries). They own tunnel-boring machines, marine barges and piling rigs, and clients will not risk a tunnel or a breakwater on an untested bidder. **Difficulty earns a margin of about 10–15%**, but these jobs are long, sites are often delayed by approvals or land, and disputes end in arbitration. Their fortunes turn on how fast big jobs start and how fast clients pay.",
